Z||000005||ChadMan||07-26-2000||10:35 AM||||You know what's funny?  My 84 was similar.  When I bought it, it ran rough and felt sluggish.  I replaced the "usual suspects" (plugs, wires, distributor cap & rotor) and ran some fuel-injector cleaner through it, then verified the timing was correct and replaced the MAP sensor.  Nothing seemed to make a difference.<P>Then, a few months later, it started improving on its own.  Eventually it idled nice and smooth and pulled strongly (for a Duke, anyway) to the redline.  I didn't care why.  I was just glad!||||reg||1
